<section class="sec sec-paper" aria-labelledby="story-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split-body reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Meet the founder</span>
        <h2 class="sec-title" id="story-h">God provided all three, <em>one door at a time</em>.</h2>

        <p class="founder-name">Keisha Ortiz</p>
        <p class="founder-role">Founder and Board Chair &nbsp;•&nbsp; Denton County, Texas</p>

        <p>Twenty years ago, I found myself experiencing something I never imagined would be part of my story: homelessness. I could not see it then, but looking back, I can see God's handprints throughout my journey. My family needed a place to stay, I needed a job, and I needed a way forward.</p>

        <p>He led us to a transitional home on Ross Avenue in Dallas, where my family found more than a roof over our heads. We found a safe place to begin rebuilding our lives. Catholic Charities of Dallas helped me obtain my green card and authorization to work. The facility had a workforce center where I could search for jobs, and a first-class childcare facility where my five-month-old son could learn and grow while I focused on finding employment.</p>

        <p>God also placed volunteers in our lives who helped us create a budget and held us accountable as we learned to make better financial decisions.</p>

        <p>So many people, so many ministries, woven together by God, carried me until I could stand on my own.</p>

        <blockquote class="pullquote">Twenty years later, I serve on the board of directors of the very facility where my son took his first steps.</blockquote>

        <p>At the time, I saw individual acts of kindness. Today, I see God's faithfulness in every provision, every person, and every open door. <strong>I did not know it then, but I was experiencing the very kind of support I would one day feel called to provide for another woman.</strong></p>
      </div>

      <div class="split-visual reveal d2">
